; effect4_engine — the OCaml host engine under the generated Lean machine
; (docs/research/2026-09-08-engine-brief.md; designs -a1-state, -a2-persistence,
; -a3-queue-query). Flat layout: every module is one `e4_*.ml` with its `.mli` and a
; property list at its head (ocaml/STANDARDS.md); tests live in test/ (their own dune).
; Dependencies: the stdlib, unix, threads, `effect4_eff` (the exact program wire, ocaml/eff —
; the generated engine opens Eff_types, the one program type), Zarith (a Lean natural is `Z.t`,
; M4) and `effect4_bytes` (bytes/: hexadecimal, SHA-256) — nothing else without a measured need
; recorded in the design that asks for it. Builds as part of the estate workspace (ocaml/dune lists
; engine; `cd ocaml && dune build engine`).

(library
 (name effect4_engine)
 (public_name effect4_engine)
 (libraries unix threads.posix zarith effect4_eff effect4_bytes effect4_lcnf)
 (flags
  (:standard -w +a-4-9-40-41-42-44-45-70 -w @55)))

; Rule 7 of ocaml/STANDARDS.md over this library's typed tree (ocaml/tools/typed_lint).

(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (deps
  (sandbox none)
  (:cmt
   (glob_files .effect4_engine.objs/byte/*.cmt)))
 (action
  (chdir
   %{workspace_root}
   (run %{exe:../tools/typed_lint/main.exe} %{cmt}))))
